#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Regenerate the Ironsworn-family adapters' content from Datasworn. Standard library only.

The Ironsworn and Ironsworn: Starforged SRDs (Shawn Tomkin, CC BY 4.0) are published
as machine-readable JSON by Datasworn (https://github.com/rsek/datasworn), along with
some rulebook text (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0; see each adapter's SOURCE.md). This tool converts
one pinned copy of each ruleset into its gm adapter's formats:

  adapters/<adapter>/oracles/**/*.md           every rollable table (`roll table` format)
  adapters/<adapter>/rules/oracles.md          an index of those tables
  adapters/<adapter>/rules/moves.md            the full move list
  adapters/<adapter>/rules/assets.md           the asset index, and
  adapters/<adapter>/rules/assets/<cat>.md     every asset card, by category
  adapters/<adapter>/rules/truths.md           the setting truths
  adapters/<adapter>/rules/encounters.md       the sample NPCs and foes
  tests/fixtures/oracles/<adapter>/**/*.json   golden ranges for tests/test_oracle_parity.py

with classic Ironsworn also getting rules/regions.md (the Ironlands atlas). The
rulesets and their adapters:

  starforged  datasworn/starforged/starforged.json  ->  adapters/starforged
  classic     datasworn/classic/classic.json        ->  adapters/ironsworn

The tool owns its output: a run deletes every file it generated before (each .md
starts with the GENERATED marker; the fixture dir is all its own) and writes the
new set, so edit this tool or its pin, never the output. Hand-written adapter files
(adapter.md, SOURCE.md, frames/, sheet-template.md, and the rulebook procedures in
rules/, such as rules/campaign-launch.md and rules/character-creation.md) have no
marker and are never touched; a generated path that would overwrite one is an error.

Each character sheet is hand-written, since a character's sheet is copied from it and
much of its layout isn't data, but its data lines (stats, condition meters, impacts or
debilities, the special tracks, the STARSHIP's integrity) are checked: a run, --check
included, fails unless sheet-template.md carries each of them verbatim (sheet_lines()
lists them).

Usage:
  datasworn-import                        fetch every pinned upstream, verify, regenerate
  datasworn-import --ruleset classic      just one ruleset
  datasworn-import --ruleset R --json F   use a local copy of R's pinned file instead
  datasworn-import --cache DIR            fetch once into DIR, reuse it after (CI caches DIR)
  datasworn-import --check                regenerate in memory and diff against the tree
                                          (exit 1 on any drift; CI runs this)

To move the pin: change UPSTREAM_REF and UPSTREAM_TAG below and each ruleset's
sha256 in RULESETS, re-run, review the diff (and ERRATA, and each ruleset's licenses), and update the
adapters' SOURCE.md files and NOTICE.
"""
